WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:16.343
Unit twenty-seven: Mixed Methods Research. Today you will express results and consequences with 'thereby'.

4
00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:19.295
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.315
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.418
Mixed methods.

7
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:31.342
Mixed methods means research combining qualitative and quantitative approaches.

8
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.820
Mixed methods suit complex social questions.

9
00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:38.115
Your turn. Say: Mixed methods.

10
00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:42.223
Mixed methods.

11
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:44.031
Qualitative.

12
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:49.141
Qualitative means concerned with meanings, experiences and descriptions.

13
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.655
Qualitative data explained the survey results.

14
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.914
Your turn. Say: Qualitative.

15
00:00:58.767 --> 00:00:59.826
Qualitative.

16
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:01.666
Quantitative.

17
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.706
Quantitative means concerned with numerical measurement.

18
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:09.048
Quantitative data showed the scale of the problem.

19
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.244
Your turn. Say: Quantitative.

20
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.962
Quantitative.

21
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:17.973
Triangulation.

22
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:23.525
Triangulation means cross-checking findings using different methods or sources.

23
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.393
Triangulation increased confidence in the conclusions.

24
00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.392
Your turn. Say: Triangulation.

25
00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:34.536
Triangulation.

26
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:36.226
Interview.

27
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:41.143
Interview means a conversation designed to elicit detailed information.

28
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.085
Follow-up interviews explored unexpected findings.

29
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:48.011
Your turn. Say: Interview.

30
00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:51.891
Interview.

31
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:53.814
Statistics.

32
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:58.395
Statistics means numerical data and the methods for analysing it.

33
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.227
The statistics revealed a gender gap.

34
00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:04.597
Your turn. Say: Statistics.

35
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:08.678
Statistics.

36
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:10.627
Integration.

37
00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:16.112
Integration means the combining of different data into a unified analysis.

38
00:02:16.717 --> 00:02:19.750
Integration is the hardest part of mixed methods.

39
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.909
Your turn. Say: Integration.

40
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:26.907
Integration.

41
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.477
Depth.

42
00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:32.609
Depth means thoroughness of understanding beyond the surface.

43
00:02:33.217 --> 00:02:35.390
Interviews added depth to the numbers.

44
00:02:35.983 --> 00:02:38.322
Your turn. Say: Depth.

45
00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:41.936
Depth.

46
00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:46.291
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.646
Visal, why did you use both a survey and interviews in your study of student stress?

48
00:02:52.750 --> 00:03:02.194
The survey showed how widespread stress was, while the interviews explained why. The study combined methods, thereby increasing validity.

49
00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:06.154
Did the two sets of data ever contradict each other?

50
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:18.308
Once. The survey suggested exams were the main cause, but interviews revealed family expectations, thereby changing our interpretation.

51
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:21.230
So integration was essential?

52
00:03:22.317 --> 00:03:28.928
Exactly. We presented both side by side, thereby showing the full picture rather than half of it.

53
00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.602
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.809
Grammar focus: Linking with thereby.

55
00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:36.273
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:40.074
The study combined methods, thereby increasing validity.

57
00:03:40.983 --> 00:03:45.340
The interviews revealed family pressure, thereby changing our interpretation.

58
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.351
We presented both data sets together, thereby showing the full picture.

59
00:03:51.300 --> 00:04:00.004
'Thereby' means 'by doing this'. It links an action to its direct result and is followed by an -ing form. It is formal and common in academic writing.

60
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.457
Be careful! Don't say: We combined methods, thereby increase validity.

61
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.153
Say: We combined methods, thereby increasing validity.

62
00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:13.568
After 'thereby', use the -ing form.

63
00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:17.019
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:19.763
Numbers and Stories Together.

65
00:04:20.063 --> 00:04:25.871
For decades, researchers argued over whether numbers or narratives offered the truer picture of social reality.

66
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:33.115
Mixed methods research rejects this choice, combining statistics with interviews to answer complex questions.

67
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.898
A typical study combines methods, thereby increasing validity through triangulation.

68
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:46.323
Quantitative data reveals the scale of a phenomenon, whereas qualitative data uncovers the reasons behind it.

69
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:53.698
The real challenge lies in integration, since the two kinds of evidence must be woven into one coherent argument.

70
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.732
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:02.488
The study combined methods, thereby blank validity.

72
00:05:02.788 --> 00:05:06.755
A, increase. B, increasing. C, increased.

73
00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.729
The answer is B: increasing.

74
00:05:13.883 --> 00:05:16.080
'Thereby' is closest in meaning to blank.

75
00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.846
A, by doing this. B, despite this. C, before this.

76
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.550
The answer is A: by doing this.

77
00:05:27.717 --> 00:05:30.564
Which data type reveals the scale of a phenomenon?

78
00:05:30.864 --> 00:05:34.935
A, qualitative. B, quantitative. C, narrative.

79
00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.952
The answer is B: quantitative.

80
00:05:42.117 --> 00:05:44.871
Cross-checking findings with different methods is blank.

81
00:05:45.171 --> 00:05:49.010
A, integration. B, triangulation. C, depth.

82
00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.344
The answer is B: triangulation.

83
00:05:56.483 --> 00:06:00.561
According to the reading, where does the real challenge of mixed methods lie?

84
00:06:00.861 --> 00:06:05.223
A, in integration. B, in sampling. C, in statistics alone.

85
00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:11.277
The answer is A: in integration.

86
00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:15.537
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:16.383 --> 00:06:18.894
When is a mixed methods approach most useful?

88
00:06:35.683 --> 00:06:37.091
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:37.391 --> 00:07:10.330
A mixed methods approach is most useful when a question has both a 'how much' and a 'why' dimension. For example, a survey might show that forty percent of students skip breakfast, while interviews explain the reasons, thereby giving policymakers a complete picture. It is also valuable when one method's findings are surprising and need further explanation. On the other hand, it demands more time, money and expertise than a single approach. Therefore, I would only use it when the question genuinely requires both.

90
00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.420
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:13.317 --> 00:07:17.258
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and linking with thereby.

92
00:07:17.558 --> 00:07:22.253
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

93
00:07:22.553 --> 00:07:25.241
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:07:25.541 --> 00:07:28.019
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

